<% slot :hero do %>
  <%= render Hero.new(badge: "Case study", badge_url: projects_url, title: "A CRM that had to keep running without a pause") do |hero| %>
    <% hero.slot :lede do %>
      <a href="https://www.bomae.dk/">Bomae</a> runs its entire business
      &mdash; leads, contracts, advisory work, and invoicing &mdash; through
      one internal CRM, built up over ten years. When the employee behind it
      changed jobs, a new developer had to take over operations without any
      disruption.
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<%= markdown(<<~MARKDOWN)
  ## The handover

  The system was in good shape and worked well, but was only documented
  in the code itself. Substance Lab was hired to take over development
  and operations, working closely with Bomae's management. To get
  through the handover safely, without prior knowledge of the system,
  every change was kept as narrow as possible and backed by
  test-driven development. That preserved employees' existing workflows
  and avoided disruptions along the way.
MARKDOWN
%>

<aside class="factbox pull-right">
  <div class="factbox-body">
    <h2>Who is Bomae?</h2>
